.TH MIRACAST 1 "2026" "miracast 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
miracast \- Wi-Fi Display (Miracast) source and sink for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B miracast
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Implements the Wi-Fi Display RTSP control protocol (messages M1\(emM7, keep-alive,
IDR request, teardown), Wi-Fi Direct group formation through
.BR wpa_supplicant (8),
and an H.264/MPEG-TS/RTP media path through GStreamer.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
List Wi-Fi Display devices found nearby.
.TP
.BI cast " name|MAC"
Stream the screen to a sink.
.TP
.B sink
Receive and display a stream.
.SH OPTIONS
See
.B miracast --help.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Root (or CAP_NET_ADMIN) for group addressing; wpa_supplicant with P2P enabled
and a P2P-capable driver; dnsmasq (sink as group owner); a DHCP client;
GStreamer base, good, bad, ugly and libav plugins.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses
.BR sysexits.h (3)
values: 0 success, 64 usage, 69 service unavailable, 70 protocol error,
71 OS error, 75 temporary failure, 68 sink not found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wpa_supplicant (8),
.BR gst-launch-1.0 (1)
